---
import PortalApp from "../components/PortalApp.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="DevRel Activity Reporting & Analytics MCP Server"
  canonicalPath="/"
>
  <PortalApp />

  <section class="card" aria-labelledby="how-it-works">
    <h2 id="how-it-works" style="margin-top:0;">🚀 Connect Any AI Agent to Your DevRel Workflow</h2>
    <p style="color:var(--text-muted);">
      DevRel MCP (`https://devrel.codingcat.dev/mcp`) implements the official <strong>MCP Streamable HTTP</strong> and
      <strong>MCP OAuth 2.1</strong> specifications (Protected Resource Metadata, Dynamic Client Registration, PKCE S256,
      and per-user AES-256-GCM encrypted Cloudflare D1 storage).
    </p>

    <div class="grid-3">
      <article class="card" style="margin-bottom:0; background:rgba(15,22,38,0.65);">
        <h3 style="margin-top:0; font-size:1.05rem;">1. Claude Code & Cursor</h3>
        <p style="font-size:0.88rem; color:var(--text-muted);">
          Add the remote Streamable HTTP endpoint. Your editor will automatically launch OAuth 2.1 login & consent:
        </p>
        <pre><code>claude mcp add --transport http \
  devrel https://devrel.codingcat.dev/mcp</code></pre>
      </article>

      <article class="card" style="margin-bottom:0; background:rgba(15,22,38,0.65);">
        <h3 style="margin-top:0; font-size:1.05rem;">2. Auto-Pull Content Stats</h3>
        <p style="font-size:0.88rem; color:var(--text-muted);">
          Ask your AI assistant to fetch your latest YouTube video views, Dev.to reads, Hashnode posts, or GitHub releases and submit them to GDE & MVP in one prompt.
        </p>
        <pre><code>"Fetch my latest YouTube video stats
and submit it to both Google GDE
and Microsoft MVP."</code></pre>
      </article>

      <article class="card" style="margin-bottom:0; background:rgba(15,22,38,0.65);">
        <h3 style="margin-top:0; font-size:1.05rem;">3. Multi-Program Support</h3>
        <p style="font-size:0.88rem; color:var(--text-muted);">
          Built for Google Developer Experts (GDE), Microsoft MVPs, AWS Community Builders, Docker Captains, Cypress Ambassadors, and custom Advocu programs.
        </p>
        <a href="/docs" class="btn secondary" style="width:100%;">Explore All 19 MCP Tools →</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
